index 0000000..2e700d7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/still-prototron.md
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Still core test release
+
+This onboards `still-platform-pilot` on Prototron using the supported
+`proto onboard still-platform-pilot reve-ai/still-platform-pilot --disable-debug-agent`
+flow. The application repository remains to be created.
+
+The selected release serves the native Still interface and a selected Forma
+document workflow from one application backend with fresh test data. Paid models,
+uploads, background indexing and Memory are disabled for the first release.
+
+## Infrastructure in this change
+
+- Namespace, Kubernetes service account and namespace-scoped CI `edit` binding.
+- Standard prototype Google service account, repository-specific GitHub workload
+  identity binding, KSA binding, cluster viewer and registry writer permissions.
+- Restricted Pod Security and resource quota: six pods, one 5Gi PVC, 1 requested
+  CPU / 2Gi requested memory, 4 CPU / 3Gi memory limits.
+- Custom route for `still-platform-pilot.p.reve-dev.com`: `/api` to `api:80`,
+  other paths to `frontend:80`, through the shared IAP-protected gateway.
+- Default deny, with the inherited namespace network allowances restricted to
+  `app=api` and `app=web`. PostgreSQL receives no inherited ingress allowance;
+  the application deployment supplies its API-only port-5432 policy. This avoids
+  additive network policies reopening the database to the gateway or web pod.
+
+This follows the current prototype convention of a shared workload/CI Google
+identity. It does not create application workloads, passwords, object storage,
+admissions, or a working application URL. It does not change shared IAP access.
+
+## Release prerequisites
+
+The user authorized a **$200 total infrastructure spending ceiling** for this
+test. Resource quotas are capacity limits, not a billing cap. Billing/cleanup
+owner is `westbrook.johnson@reve.art`. Expiry and live IAP admission verification are
+still unresolved. Record those values and a cost-control procedure before
+deploying billable workloads.
+One IAP operator can create and select multiple app test users for app-level
+sharing/revocation acceptance. Each has separate app permissions and content.
+This does not qualify isolation between independent Google accounts.
+
+After infrastructure review/merge, a maintainer applies
+`terraform/reve-prototyping` through the normal process. Create the private app
+repository and protected deployment environment, fresh credentials and private
+bucket, then enable the verified-main GitHub-to-GKE workflow. Retain the secrets
+and PVC across ordinary redeploys. The app validates signed IAP assertions and
+its own named admissions, roles and consent; it rejects access after the release
+expiry. An operator must remove the resources to stop their ongoing charges.
+
+The test requires actual hosted verification of sign-in, persistence, the same
+document edited in Still and Forma, sharing/revocation, deletion, pod restart
+and an ordinary redeploy. A redirect to shared Google sign-in alone does not
+prove that the application is deployed.
+
+## Validation
+
+```sh
+kubectl kustomize k8s/prototron/user-namespaces/still-platform-pilot
+terraform fmt -check terraform/reve-prototyping/user-namespaces.tf
+python3 -m unittest discover -s experiments/proto/tests -q
+git diff --check
+```
+
+No Terraform plan/apply or cluster mutation was performed while preparing this PR.
